Package: enfs-dkms
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 dkms (>= 2.8),
 build-essential,
 linux-headers-generic | linux-headers
Recommends: nfs-common
Description: Enhanced NFS multipath client (DKMS source) for Ubuntu 26.04
 enfs is the OpenEuler "Enhanced NFS" client, providing multipath mounts,
 round-robin RPC dispatch and transport failover on top of the in-tree
 Linux NFS client.
 .
 This package ships the source under /usr/src/enfs-<ver>/ and registers
 it with DKMS, which builds replacement nfs.ko, sunrpc.ko and the new
 enfs.ko on package install and on every kernel upgrade. The replacement
 modules are placed in /lib/modules/$(uname -r)/updates/ and take
 precedence over the in-tree Ubuntu modules.
 .
 Removing this package via "apt purge enfs-dkms" restores the stock
 Ubuntu nfs.ko and sunrpc.ko.
